  "note": "All 29 gameplay buildings were viewed together in the actual candidate WebGL gallery from isometric, front and back. Dark tiled roofs, timber framing, pale infill and warm window details form a consistent Kyoto-inspired family, visibly distinct from Alpine and the other regions. The three upgrade levels remain readable and public buildings share the same finish. Actual candidate game was exercised at 360x740: entry fee, coin toss, AI purchase of a double lot, manual event acknowledgements, player-turn availability and overview toggle. The local and overview screens show regional far houses, pink trees and water around the board. Confirm controls fit the narrow screen and appear on the right. Browser console inspection reported no errors/warnings. The old native exit confirmation stalled browser automation after these checks; it is tracked separately for replacement and is not represented as passed. No physical-phone performance benchmark is claimed.",
